Hey, check it out -- we're not dead!  ;)  But yeah, there was a fairly
long break in there between updates; real life spent a bit of time
intervening, and this ended up suffering.  I did break save
compatibility with this version to get the new resistance variances in;
other than that, the changelog is mostly self-explanatory.

Also, tomorrow (7/8) will be the first year's anniversary of this fork;
in that time, over 12,000 games have been played on the public server,
and some unknown number of people have downloaded the Windows binary
and/or source .diff (I don't bother tracking, so all I can say is "more
than ten and less than 12,000").  This was somewhat of an experiment in
the initial run, but you guys have given it a lot of support; thanks
greatly for all of it.  Without you, it would not have continued this
far.

The code is also now available from anonymous svn (see website for
details), which means you can go back through my logs and see how many
one-liner typos I made over the course of all this.  :P  Anyway, enjoy;
here we go again!

Changelog follows:

7/6:
DR: Minimum resistance obtained from any corpse halved; amount of 
	"eating" required to get 100% resistance doubled.  (Still too 
	many people obtaining a full set well before Gehennom.)
DR: If you leave bones, you may leave a skull behind.
DR: If you are struck by a footrice's hissing attack, the stoning 
	process will begin much more frequently, regardless of moon phase.  
	This should make them actually somewhat dangerous while alive.
DR: Hostile priests of sufficient level may summon minions to help them.

6/30:
DR: Fix bug where chaotic Knight sacrificing empty-handed would segfault
DR: Fix helm-of-clarity interaction with hallucinations
DR: Stunning attacks now stop player occupation -- will prevent 
	wandering around aimlessly from being stunned while in travel mode
DR: Things without hands can't pick up big piles of _anything_ now.
DR: Hallucination no longer shows on the status line (it should be obvious, 
	really): this saves room for statuses that aren't so obvious, like "Ill".
DR: New intrinsic: vulnerability to fire, cold, electricity, or acid.
-- You will take a significantly larger amount of damage from the 
	corresponding element if vulnerable.
-- Even if you are fully or partially resistant to the element, you will 
	still take some amount of damage if you are vulnerable; the more 
	resistance, the less damage.
-- Currently there is only one way to acquire the intrinsic, but be warned; 
	it may be more commonly available than you think.

